00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.950
I think they will do a beautiful little sky.

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.450
I like bright, shiny little skies.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:16.750
I'm gonna put a little more black in there.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:23.110
There, that's better, that's better here.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:27.140
I'm sorta creating a little downward angle, very lightly.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.930
As we work down in the sky, I want it to get...

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.060
lighter and lighter in color.

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:34.950
So if you start at the top,

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.130
when you have the most paint on your brush

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:37.750
and work downward,

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.570
automatically it'll mix with the liquid white

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:41.290
and that'll happen.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:42.610
There we go.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.940
Maybe a little touch right in there.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.780
See how it's getting lighter and lighter?

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:48.980
